  "dom_id": "step-q354923",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "A scientist bought $1$ fluid ounce of a chemical solution and paid $\\$1.60$ for it. What's the unit price per cup?\n\nAssume that there are $8$ fluid ounces in one cup.",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that there are $8$ fluid ounces in each cup.  \n\nSince the price is $\\$1.60$ per fluid ounce, to find the price per cup, we multiply by $8:$\n\n$$\n1.60\\times 8=12.80\n$$\n\nTherefore, the chemical solution costs $\\$12.80$ per cup.",
